From c8d3e78f18c4afb7f3dc06920600770914657afe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 23:45:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland.drv: Bound WM_CANCELMODE on keyboard leave.

keyboard_handle_leave() runs on the Wayland event reader thread. When
keyboard focus leaves the foreground window it sends WM_CANCELMODE to
that window with send_message(), which waits for the window's thread to
reply. A target that is busy, for instance tearing down a window tree,
therefore stalls Wayland event dispatch for the whole process until it
returns to its message loop. The send itself is not upstream behavior;
it comes from the wayland hotfix series this tree is built on.

Send the message with SendNotifyMessage semantics instead. The reader
thread never owns the target window, so the call queues the message and
returns at once, and the target still receives WM_CANCELMODE the next
time it processes sent messages. A timeout is not an option here: win32u
cancels sends that time out, which would drop WM_CANCELMODE for exactly
the busy targets that need it.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_keyboard.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_keyboard.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_keyboard.c
index 413977177e5..6a55e4d562d 100644
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_keyboard.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_keyboard.c
@@ -1047,7 +1047,7 @@ static void keyboard_handle_leave(void *private, struct wl_keyboard *wl_keyboard
     else if (hwnd == foreground || wayland_is_menu_popup(hwnd))
     {
         if (!(NtUserGetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_STYLE) & WS_MINIMIZE))
-            send_message(hwnd, WM_CANCELMODE, 0, 0);
+            NtUserMessageCall(hwnd, WM_CANCELMODE, 0, 0, NULL, NtUserSendNotifyMessage, FALSE);
     }
 
     if (hwnd == foreground)
